The VM provenance primitive is landed on `exception-vm-provenance`, pushed to origin.

## What changed (strictly the VM surface)

- **`yin.vm/module.cljc`** — the `cell` module gains the two compiler-private doors `cell/dsg__new-provenance` (`:cell/new-provenance`, arity `[2]`) and `cell/dsg__provenance` (`:cell/provenance`, arity `[1]`), each an `:effectful` profile.
- **`yin.vm/engine.cljc`** — `heap-write` preserves `:provenance` while updating `:value`/`:seal`; `:cell/new-provenance` installs `:value`+`:seal`+`:provenance` atomically; `:cell/provenance` authenticates before consulting the slot and returns nil otherwise (never fatal, never mutating). GC traces `:provenance` as data from live entries, pinned entries, and as an extra allocation root (`count-allocation` now `& roots`).
- **`yin.vm.cljc`** — `reserved-prefix` ("dsg__") + `reserved-prefix-name?`.
- **`yin.vm/macro.cljc`** — the expander prelude refuses compiler-private names in `yin/variable`, `yin/lambda`/`yin/make-lambda`, and `yin/make-def`, closing the macro hole.
- **`yin.vm/docs/state.md`** — heap-entry shape (:119) documents `:provenance`.

## Verification

- New `yin.vm.provenance-test` (13 tests / 131 assertions): mint/read, write-once, query-nil, set!-preserves, content-copy-loses, ref-copy-retains; GC probes (ordinary/pinned/allocation-triggered + eventual reclamation); macro-door + exported-helper bypass — **0 failures**.
- Existing seam suites green: cell, heap-reclamation, module, effect-forgery, rule-r, parity, mint, de Bruijn stack+register, semantic, macro, linker-manifest/require.
- `clj -M:kondo --lint` on changed files: **0 errors** (one pre-existing "Redundant let expression" warning in `macro/construct`, untouched).
- Did **not** run `yang.call.exception-contract-test` locally (owner ruling).

